<p>The United Arab Emirates briefly closed its airspace early on March 17 after a new wave of Iranian missile and drone attacks tied to the widening US-Israel-Iran war, then reopened it as air traffic returned to normal. The flare-up pushed the conflict deeper into the Gulf, with reports of explosions in Dubai and Doha and repeated strikes hitting sites in the UAE, including the Fujairah oil hub. In Abu Dhabi, debris from an intercepted Iranian missile killed one person. Several reports identified the victim as a Pakistani national, while another said he was Palestinian, highlighting discrepancies in early reporting. Israeli military reporting said Iran launched a fresh missile salvo, while the broader conflict was described as having begun on February 28, when the US and Israel attacked Iran, and as reaching its 18th day by March 17. Even with the disruption, the reopening of UAE airspace brought some short-term relief for travelers and regional transport.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/XYvuJQK4GYZuNsGEUi_biXnOZ8KAHLLZx-hbiHkCT67RXbBwuI2NS96_tGqKnZP7uoC0jxNcLuPZt7hfxCXgBW-l5TK1OW1OEBk9IwWm0iWBXcTE1RdleXPyQ3gSRieZxJtmBCz6RD8W-YKNE6oFxe5LzMd0ffJ9JQpnv9Uy1w_joNSBdy3F0wU4JekyK7ZxbxAyxlXqTYghH5SX3R0yPBFRq_4f0aPX2vRP5bkcs_bbGxs' alt='Image related to the March 17 escalation in the Gulf during the US-Israel-Iran war.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Airport disruptions: Dubai International Airport has come under repeated pressure since the war began, showing how a regional conflict is now directly affecting one of the world’s busiest aviation hubs.</li><li>Oil site fire: A drone strike sparked a fire at a UAE oil facility linked to the Fujairah hub, adding energy infrastructure to the growing list of Gulf targets hit during the conflict.</li><li>Broader theatre: Firstpost said the war had entered its third week, with attacks intensifying across Lebanon, Iraq, and the Gulf alongside rising diplomatic pressure and global security concerns.</li><li>Air defences active: Euronews said the UAE’s air defences were intercepting Iranian fire during the brief closure, suggesting the airspace restriction overlapped with live defensive operations.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UAE authorities: By reopening airspace once the immediate threat passed, officials signaled confidence in the country’s interception and air-traffic management during short high-risk periods. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-reopens-airspace-after-brief-shutdown-amid-iran-strikes'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Israeli military: Israel said Iran had launched a fresh missile salvo and that warning sirens sounded south of the Sea of Galilee, framing the attacks as part of an ongoing exchange across several fronts. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/uae-briefly-closes-airspace-iran-israel-as-west-asia-conflict-escalates/article70752403.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera: Its reporting stressed that repeated drone strikes on the Fujairah oil hub show the war is spreading instability across the Gulf and putting strategic infrastructure at risk. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/17/drone-sparks-fire-at-uae-oil-site-as-gulf-takes-more-hits-amid-iran-war'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-israel-iran-war-live-news-updates-donald-trump-mojtaba-khamenei-dubai-uae-baghdad-kuwait-airport-11217035#publisher=newsstand'>Iran War Live Updates: Pak National Killed Due To Missile Debris In Abu Dhabi</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/uae-reopens-airspace-after-brief-shutdown-amid-iran-strikes'>UAE reopens airspace after brief shutdown amid Iran strikes</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/17/drone-sparks-fire-at-uae-oil-site-as-gulf-takes-more-hits-amid-iran-war'>Drone sparks fire at UAE oil site as Gulf takes more hits amid Iran war</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><